# .dockerignore — keep the runtime image build context lean.
#
# Phase 21 D-02 / Plan 21-03 Task 1; relocated from distribution/docker/.dockerignore
# to repo root post-PR-#196 CodeRabbit #17 — docker buildx resolves .dockerignore
# relative to the BUILD CONTEXT ROOT (not the Dockerfile location). The deploy.yml
# docker_publish job uses `context: .` + `file: distribution/docker/Dockerfile`,
# so the canonical home for these exclusions is repo root.
#
# Build-context discipline rationale:
#   - The runtime Dockerfile only needs `_output/linux-${TARGETARCH}/` (for the
#     runtime stage COPY) and `distribution/docker/root/` (for the s6-overlay
#     scripts). The Chromium source is now the official playwright/dotnet builder
#     image (Phase 33.3 — Playwright .NET port), so NO build-context input is
#     needed for Chromium provisioning (the old tools/ChromiumPrefetch PuppeteerSharp
#     BrowserFetcher helper was retired).
#   - Everything else is noise that bloats the buildx context upload.
#   - `_output/` is excluded as a whole, then the per-arch subtree is
#     re-included via explicit COPY in the Dockerfile (Docker treats COPY paths
#     against the build context, so the file must be present even when
#     .dockerignore excludes its parent — buildx does this correctly).
#
# Sonarr divergence: this file is the only docker build context for the
# Mangarr.Core runtime image. The existing distribution/docker-build/Dockerfile
# is the legacy Debian-package builder (different image, invoked from a different
# pipeline path) and is not affected by this exclusion list.

# ─── VCS ───
.git/
.gitignore
.gitattributes
.gitkeep
.github/

# ─── Planning + docs (massive, never needed at build time) ───
.planning/
docs/
*.md
!distribution/docker/**/*.md
DIVERGENCE.md
README.md
PROJECT_CONTEXT.md
CLAUDE.md
**/CLAUDE.md

# ─── Test output + dev artifacts ───
_tests/
.playwright-mcp/
TestResult.xml
TestResult.html
**/*.trx

# ─── Node / frontend dev ───
frontend/node_modules/
**/node_modules/
yarn-error.log
npm-debug.log

# ─── .NET dev artifacts ───
**/bin/
**/obj/
**/*.user
**/*.suo
**/.vs/
**/AppPackages/
**/BundleArtifacts/

# ─── Editor / IDE ───
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
*.swo
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# ─── Docker self-exclusion (avoid pulling our own build context in) ───
distribution/docker-build/_output/
distribution/docker-build/_artifacts/

# ─── Output that is NOT the per-arch published artifacts ───
# _output/ wholesale-excluded; the Dockerfile COPYs _output/linux-${TARGETARCH}/
# AND _output/UI/ explicitly, so both must be re-included as exceptions. Without
# the UI re-include the buildx context filter silently drops the SPA bundle and
# the Dockerfile COPY fails with "failed to compute cache key ... not found".
_output/
!_output/linux-amd64/
!_output/linux-arm64/
!_output/UI/

# ─── Misc transient ───
*.log
*.tmp
*.bak
*.cbz.tmp
.playwright-report/
playwright-report/
